  "comment": "Each scenario is one screenshot: a screen of the launcher, the player's games (title IDs), whether the setup is done and whether a controller is connected; the game of a sheet or of its settings page, with the page's category (one of nxnative's sections), or the game being installed with work: installing, or its install that failed, with the report to copy, with work: install-failed, or a new version of Cartouche on offer with work: update, a newer build of one of the player's games in their games folder with work: newer-build (the sheet's game, or the first of the player's); the Apple ID sign-in, with Apple's request for a verification code with work: code; a certificate iOS no longer accepts, with work: certificate. A scenario with a width and a height is drawn at that size in points, with the safe area of that iPhone, on an iPad: the iPhone 17 Pro, and the iPhone Duo folded (466 x 678) and unfolded (626 x 890), from Apple's pixel sizes at 3x. A scenario with a device takes the whole screen of that simulator, with its own safe area and system bars; a landscape one turns the gallery sideways, as a game does, while the simulator stays upright.",
